Package: lmmresample
Title: Resampling Inference for Mixed Models of Densely Sampled Time Series
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ricardo", "Martínez-Flores", , "ricardo.antonio.martinezf@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8435-2710")),
    person("Hans", "Supèr", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Permutation and bootstrap inference for linear and generalized
    linear (mixed-effects) models fitted to block-structured repeated
    measurements, such as densely sampled physiological time series
    (pupillometry, eye movements, EEG, fNIRS, heart rate, electrodermal
    activity, electromyography) or features extracted from them per trial or
    per participant. Resampling operates on whole trials or participants, so
    dependence within blocks is preserved. Provides permutation tests under
    user-declared exchangeability, simulation-based calibration of the
    permutation null, family-wise error control with the max-t procedure,
    bootstrap confidence intervals (percentile and bias-corrected and
    accelerated) and leave-one-subject-out diagnostics.
